  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_5' aria-label=\" Zubair. P versus State of Kerala & Ors. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('5','2026','2026_3_125_143','2026INSC151'); ><font size='4'> <strong>ZUBAIR. P<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>STATE OF KERALA & ORS. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 3 S.C.R. 125</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 151</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010000672026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : K.V. VISWANATHAN<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup></strong><br> Issue for Consideration Issue arose for consideration whether r.6(2)(24)(iii) of Chapter XXXII of the Kerala Education Rules mandates that the State Eligibility Test-SET qualification must be in the concerned subject only for appointment as Higher Secondary School Teachers-HSST or in any subject so, whether the appellant satisfies the said requirement or qualifies for exemption u/r.10(4) of Chapter XXXII of the Rules. Headnotes&dagger; Kerala Education Rules &ndash; Chapter XXXII, r.6(2)(24)(iii) &ndash; Interpretation &ndash; Essential qualifications for appointment as Higher Secondary<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 13-02-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 1620/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('5','2026','2026_3_125_143','2026INSC151','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-se